{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevLogAsymptotic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.KashaevLogAsymptotic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevPeakValue","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevArgmax","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevTailBound"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.le_log_kashaev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.le_log_kashaev","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevLogAsymptotic.lean#L184-L198","doc":"**`⟨4₁⟩_N` from below, additively.**  `log(m·e^{−1}) = log m − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_kashaev_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_kashaev_le","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevLogAsymptotic.lean#L168-L182","doc":"**`⟨4₁⟩_N` from above, additively.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.four_le_kashaevUpperConst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.four_le_kashaevUpperConst","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevLogAsymptotic.lean#L149-L166","doc":"It is at least `4` — the two window terms alone contribute that much. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevUpperConst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevUpperConst","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevLogAsymptotic.lean#L140-L147","doc":"The explicit constant from `kashaev_le_argmax_mul`, named so it can be\nlogged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_kashaevProd_argmax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_kashaevProd_argmax","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevLogAsymptotic.lean#L106-L133","doc":"**The peak value, with every constant explicit.**  `log_kashaevProd_saddle`\ninstantiated at `k = ⌊5N/6⌋` and `M = 4`.\n\n`M = 4` is not an estimate: `1/sin²` is exactly `4` at the saddle and smaller\neverywhere else on `[π/6, 5π/6]`, so it is the sharp constant for this\ninterval. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.argmax_angle_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.argmax_angle_mem","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevLogAsymptotic.lean#L84-L104","doc":"`θ_{k*} ∈ [π/6, 5π/6]`, so `half_le_sin` applies to the whole interval\nbetween it and the saddle — and hence `M = 4` works. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.argmax_offset_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.argmax_offset_le","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevLogAsymptotic.lean#L66-L82","doc":"The offset is at most one step, as `log_kashaevProd_saddle` requires. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.argmax_angle_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.argmax_angle_eq","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevLogAsymptotic.lean#L49-L64","doc":"`θ_{k*} = 5π/6 − rπ/(6N)`: the saddle index undershoots the saddle angle by\nexactly the remainder's share of one step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_argmax_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_argmax_pos","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevLogAsymptotic.lean#L34-L41","doc":"The peak term is positive — it is at least `N²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}